## Mandatory rules

- Confirm the goal, constraints, non-goals, affected modules, acceptance criteria, and verification before implementation.
- Preserve existing uncommitted work. Do not reset, clean, overwrite, commit, or reformat unrelated files.
- Keep the verified architecture and dependency direction: {{ARCHITECTURE_SUMMARY}}
- Use only confirmed project commands. Do not install dependencies or change configuration without task authorization.
- Add or update tests in proportion to changed behavior.
- Completion requires applicable verification from `docs/VERIFICATION.md`.
- Finish with `git diff --check`, relevant diff/status review, and a report of unverified items and residual risk.

## Workflow entrypoints

- New feature or fix: define the task with `docs/TASK_TEMPLATE.md`, then follow `docs/CODEX_WORKFLOW.md`.
- Build and test: use `$build-and-test` or follow `docs/VERIFICATION.md`.
- Review: use `$code-review`; a review-only request does not authorize fixes.
- Skill maintenance: follow `docs/SKILLS_SPEC.md`.
